Phase 4 (Months 15 – 19)- Autonomous Post-Production & Financial Safeguards
This phase focuses on the post-production chain, value addition, eliminating
distress sales to achieve the goal of doubling farmers income.
1. One-Click Logistics & Value-Addition Coordination
• Autonomous Shipping Routing: At harvest time, the farmer states via voice prompt:
"My harvest containing ___ quintals of produce is ready at these coordinates." The AI
automatically calculates cargo weight, books a slot with an integrated third-party
logistics provider, and sends a vehicle straight to the farm gate.
• Value-Chain Processing: The barcoded produce is transported to a partner cold
storage facility or warehouse unit, where it undergoes automated grading, assaying,
and chemical testing. It is then moved through processing channels for custom
packaging and retail branding. The farmer can trace the stage of value addition and
location his product is at just by scanning his barcode or through Farmer ID.
• The final end product is then stored at warehouse repository and then listed for
sale/ auction where the buyers either wholesalers, retailers or for export.
• Here the app manages end to end services of whole value addition, logistics and sale
Without farmers having to worry about any step. The transactions are fully
transparent & secured. The App takes care of all regulatory and legal compliances
with little to no involvement of the farmers. Everything is traceable through unique
digital Id and barcode of the farmer/ co operative.
16
2. Financial Safety Nets & Transparent Liquidation
• Eliminating Distress Selling: Once ingested into a registered warehouse, the
facility issues an Electronic Negotiable Warehouse Receipt (e-NWR) via the
WDRA portal. The app uses this to unlock a short-term Warehouse Receipt
Loan from partner financial institutions, providing instant cash flow so the
farmer can hold their crop until market prices peak.
• Escrow-Backed Open Auctions: B2B buyers and global exporters bid on the
branded produce through an automated interface integrated with the
Electronic National Agriculture Market (e-NAM) portal. Funds from the
winning bidder are secured within an Escrow Account, releasing directly to
the farmer's verified bank account only after shipment delivery and quality
parameters are digitally confirmed.
• Infrastructure Modernization Scaling: Matured farmer cohorts are guided
through advanced, high-yield infrastructure setups, including automated
polyhouses, hydroponic grids, and climate-controlled livestock facilities, to
continually maximize net farm income.
SCALABILITY:-
Our solution features a low marginal cost for expansion. Because we build on top of India's
existing Digital Public Infrastructure (DPI) like AgriStack, MEGHDOOT, SHC, E-NAM
etc., expanding our platform to a new district or state requires zero physical infrastructure
spending. We are scaling a software layer, not a brick-and-mortar operation. This allows us to
rapidly scale from a handful of farmers / co-operative/ FPO in Gulbarga to millions of
smallholders across India.
 Only two things change by state: the land-record connector and the local crop
knowledge base. The engine, voice layer and workflows stay the same, and AgriStack
is built as a federated architecture managed jointly by Centre and States.
 The building blocks are national. e-NAM already links 1,656 mandis and has over
1.80 crore farmers and 4,724 FPOs registered. e-NWR pledge loans are available on
Jan Samarth’s e-Kisan Upaj Nidhi, with KCC farmers eligible for pledge loans at 7%
a year, with margin generally 25%, and a credit guarantee scheme supports lenders.
 Cooperative-first scaling. Adding an FPO or cooperative adds many farmers at once
and spreads the cost of coordination.
